{"museum":"Q5647064","name":"Hancock Shaker Village","checked":"2026-11-05","source":"Hancock Shaker Village Walking Tour Map and website; Wikimedia Commons","onViewKnown":true,"note":"Hancock Shaker Village is the 1791 “City of Peace” of the Shakers: twenty historic buildings on a working farm, with about fifty room settings drawn from a collection of more than 22,000 objects. This guide lists the buildings from the Village’s own pages, room settings and objects photographed inside them, and the 2026 exhibitions. The online collection database does not allow robots, so single objects are not listed.","works":[{"id":"hsv-visitor-center","title":"Visitor Center & Center for Shaker Studies","artist":"Hancock Shaker Village","medium":"Visitor center and galleries","url":"https://hancockshakervillage.org/visit/","onView":true,"gallery":"Visitor Center","floor":"G"},{"id":"hsv-x-peculiar-grace-on-exhibit-till-december-28","title":"Peculiar Grace","artist":"Exhibition","date":"Through December 28, 2026 (Believer’s Room, free)","medium":"Exhibition","url":"https://hancockshakervillage.org/exhibition/peculiar-grace-on-exhibit-till-december-28/","imageUrl":"data/hsv/images/hsv-x-peculiar-grace-on-exhibit-till-december-28.jpg","onView":true,"gallery":"Visitor Center","floor":"G"},{"id":"hsv-laundrymachine-shop","title":"Laundry & Machine Shop","artist":"Built by the Hancock Shakers","date":"turbine of 1858","year":1858,"medium":"Historic building","url":"https://hancockshakervillage.org/shakers/museum/historic-architecture/laundrymachine-shop/","imageUrl":"data/hsv/images/hsv-laundrymachine-shop.jpg","onView":true,"gallery":"Laundry & Machine Shop","floor":"G"},{"id":"hsv-r-laundry-machine-shop-the-water-powered-machine-shop","title":"The water-powered machine shop","artist":"Room setting from the Village’s collection","medium":"Shaker objects","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Machine_Shop,_Hancock_Shaker_Village.jpg","imageUrl":"data/hsv/images/hsv-r-laundry-ma